# Layer 1 (local, fast feedback) of the `frontend-standard-check` attestation
# gate — hefesto's `.claude/skills/frontend-standard-check/SKILL.md` /
# `sdd/frontend-standard-check/design` (Engram), decision D5.
#
# Runs at pre-push, deliberately never pre-commit: the gate resolves HEAD and
# reads committed blobs via `git show <commit>:./<path>` — at pre-commit time
# the candidate bytes live in the index, not any commit, so the digest can
# never match. This mirrors why `express-ts`'s own `.husky/pre-commit`
# (`create-coliapp/.husky/pre-commit`) does not invoke its `api-standard-gate
# .mjs` either; pre-push is the earliest hook where committed bytes actually
# exist.
#
# `.husky/pre-commit` in this template is intentionally untouched by this
# change — it keeps running the fast biome/tsc/vitest subset only.
node scripts/frontend-standard-gate.mjs || exit 1
